R^2 is not comparable across rows (different variance denominators);
this shows which questions the data can answer, not a leaderboard.

Reading: the synthetic control scores high because its labels ARE a known
formula of its features plus noise -- that is a ceiling by construction, not
a result. Its only job here is to prove the training/eval code is sound, which
isolates the low real-data score as a property of the data and the horizon.
Coarsening the horizon roughly triples R^2; the nowcast rows show the features
do carry signal, so it is the step forward in time this dataset resists.
